  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 keeps the 5% figure but removes any sales bar: a model above 5% can keep being marketed indefinitely under regulator-authorised conditions, which favours Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 imposes an automatic recall above 8 per 100,000 per model with no transition, which directly hits Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), though S4's 36-month suppression deadline and S3's 24-month and 6-year shut-off timings give Northwind and Halcyon some relief. S1 is strict on timing, with 24-hour reporting for serious incidents and 10 days for others."
 },
